[h1] Animation

[p-]
Animate images by cycling through multiple viewport
regions on a single source image called a sprite sheet.
[-p]

[h2] Sprite sheets

[p-]
A sprite sheet packs multiple frames side by side in
one image file. Use viewport= and cut= to define the
frame size and the position of each frame on the sheet.
[-p]

[grid- columns=auto;auto gap=8]

[p align=center] sprite sheet
[p align=center] individual frames

[img url=podnet://48932/animation.gfx align=center]
[img url=podnet://48932/animation.gfx viewport=0_0 cut=16_16 scale=3 align=center]

[-grid]

[h2] Multiple viewports

[p-]
List frame positions in viewport= separated by
semicolons. Each entry is an X_Y position on the
source. cut=W_H defines the frame size, shared
by all frames.
[-p]

[code-]
[img url=podnet://YOUR_ID/sheet.gfx viewport=0_0;16_0 cut=16_16]
[-code]

[p] Live example - two frames cycling:

[img url=podnet://48932/animation.gfx viewport=0_0;16_0 cut=16_16 scale=4 align=center]

[h2] frames

[p-]
frames= controls how many game ticks each frame is
shown. The game runs at 60 ticks per second.
Default is 15 (4 fps).
[-p]

[code-]
[img url=podnet://YOUR_ID/s.gfx viewport=0_0;16_0 cut=16_16 frames=15]
[-code]

[p] slow (frames=30) vs fast (frames=5):

[grid- columns=auto;auto gap=8]

[p align=center] frames=30
[p align=center] frames=5

[img url=podnet://48932/animation.gfx viewport=0_0;16_0 cut=16_16 scale=4 frames=30 align=center]
[img url=podnet://48932/animation.gfx viewport=0_0;16_0 cut=16_16 scale=4 frames=5 align=center]

[-grid]

[h2] Combining with scale

[p-]
Use scale= to display small sprites at a larger size.
The frame size from cut= is scaled up before display.
[-p]

[code-]
[img url=podnet://YOUR_ID/s.gfx viewport=0_0;16_0 cut=16_16 scale=3 frames=10]
[-code]

[p] Same animation at scale=1, 2, and 3:

[grid- columns=auto;auto;auto gap=4]

[p align=center] scale=1
[p align=center] scale=2
[p align=center] scale=3

[img url=podnet://48932/animation.gfx viewport=0_0;16_0 cut=16_16 scale=1 frames=15 align=center]
[img url=podnet://48932/animation.gfx viewport=0_0;16_0 cut=16_16 scale=2 frames=15 align=center]
[img url=podnet://48932/animation.gfx viewport=0_0;16_0 cut=16_16 scale=3 frames=15 align=center]

[-grid]

[h2] Tips

[p-]
All animated images with the same frames= value stay
in sync - they advance on the same game tick.
[-p]

[p-]
A single viewport with no semicolons is always static.
viewport= and cut= work without animation too.
[-p]

[p-]
Any number of frames is supported. Just keep adding
X_Y entries separated by semicolons.
[-p]

[code-]
[img url=podnet://YOUR_ID/s.gfx viewport=0_0;16_0;32_0;48_0 cut=16_16 frames=8]
[-code]

